  "limitations": [
    "SE is the unchanged original assigned as the new source-relative visual anchor. Historical compass bearing is not recovered.",
    "The design has a single curled-wool bell body, six equally short legs in front/middle/rear left-right pairs, two eyes and two blunt cylindrical tusks; no arms, ears, tail or wings. The six-root guide is a new structural hypothesis, not a measured recovery of source 3D.",
    "Leg visibility is artistic and view-dependent: S/N show six tips, E/W show three near-side legs with three far-side legs occluded, and SW/NW/NE show five tips with one far leg occluded. Original SE retains all six visible tips. Exact source-to-new root coordinates, rigid rotation, camera elevation and 45-degree yaw increments are unproved.",
    "NE/NW small far-middle tip height does not exactly meet the schematic projection. SW/NW pixel small far-middle tips lie close to the cream hem, reducing contour separation and tiny-feature identification. Hidden attachments and precise leg depth remain approximations.",
    "Fine wool curls, face/tusk-end geometry and small foot tips simplify in pixel art. New pixels show larger curl clusters, brighter cream highlights and different line/detail density than the unchanged original SE pixel; exact color/detail-density and rigid fur-pattern matching are not established.",
